{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/586709-blue-rose-rpg-sell-me-or-scare-me","id":586709,"title":"Blue Rose RPG - sell me or scare me","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-10T19:37:09-07:00","id":586709,"title":"Blue Rose RPG - sell me or scare me","content":"Is anyone familiar with the <b>Blue Rose</b> RPG? I just ran across their kickstarter (<a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/504269797/blue-rose-the-age-roleplaying-game-of-romantic-fan?ref=nav_search\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.kickstarter.com/projects...ref=nav_search</a>) for second edition . . . and it seems like it could be interesting. However, I've never heard of it before. Can anyone recommend it? Strengths, weaknesses, etc.?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","user":"One Vorlon","date":". 07-10-2015, 10:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T21:38:59-07:00","id":586767,"title":"","content":"It's does a great job of capturing the genre it's trying to capture. If you like Mercedes Lackey and similar works of historically female audience aimed &quot;romantic fantasy&quot;, then you'll like it.<br /> <br /> It can be a bit self-congradulatory in its presentation of sexual diversity, but keep in mind it is reflecting works that WERE legitimately ahead of the curve in that regard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T14:22:53-07:00","id":591780,"title":"","content":"Hmm . . . So it places a high premium on &quot;slice of life&quot;-type material, as opposed to dungeon crawls? Interesting . . .<br /> <br /> Are there any key characters or signature storylines worth mentioning? And how does it play - I know they're going with a different game system, but did first edition play well?<br /> <br /> Also, how is the art? Judging from the kickstarter, it seems like this might be a book that places a high priority on the artwork.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/586709-blue-rose-rpg-sell-me-or-scare-me?p=586767#post586767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's does a great job of capturing the genre it's trying to capture. If you like Mercedes Lackey and similar works of historically female audience aimed &quot;romantic fantasy&quot;, then you'll like it.<br /> <br /> It can be a bit self-congradulatory in its presentation of sexual diversity, but keep in mind it is reflecting works that WERE legitimately ahead of the curve in that regard.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there any one particular book or series that <i>Blue Rose</i> takes its inspiration from? I'm seeing Tamora Pierce mentioned, also, and I'm a fan of her work (particularly <i>Wild Magic</i> and the <i>Circle of Magic</i> series). . . is that a fair comparison?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T08:10:36-07:00","id":592635,"title":"","content":"I am also interested in more details. This sounds like exactly the sort of game my wife would love.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-19T01:13:05-07:00","id":595478,"title":"","content":"Think of the default game as being more about being an official troubleshooter, rather than slice of life. You help sort out people's problems, sort out a community's problems, sort out the kingdom's problems, etc. There are monsters, but you're less likely to be fighting them as part of a dungeon crawl than you are while defending someone/somewhere.<br /> <br /> PC races in first edition were humans, Night People (orc analogues), rhydan (intelligent animals), Sea-Folk (an amphibious species who look like humans with a green or blue tint to their skin), and vata (half-elf analogues).<br /> <br /> The art's pretty good, but there're only a couple of full-page pieces in each book.<br /> <br /> First edition wasn't a game with a metaplot, offering up story outlines and story hooks rather than story lines. The new edition time skips, being set several years after first edition.<br /> <br /> The game doesn't talk about homosexuality nearly as much as you might think if you listened to the Internet. Two of the gods are in a gay relationship, Aldis is accepting of homosexuality and gay marriage, and Jarzon is hostile to it, recognising only hetero marriages (note that the game originally came out in 2005, a good decade ago).<br /> <br /> There's no particular book or series to point to; the game draws on the romantic fantasy genre, rather than one particular setting. Tamora Pierce, Mercedes Lackey's Valdemar books, Diane Duane's &quot;Door Into...&quot; series, Robin McKinley's &quot;The Blue Sword&quot; and &quot;The Hero and the Crown&quot;, Kirsten Britain's books, Elizabeth A. Lynn's &quot;Watchtower&quot;, &quot;The Dancers of Arun&quot; and &quot;The Northern Girl&quot;...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-19T14:51:10-07:00","id":596097,"title":"","content":"Interesting . . . I think I'm going to take the plunge. The stretch goals have already made the basic book a full-color hardback, and I'm always in the market for an interesting new world. Here's hoping it turns out well.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <i><u>Edit</u></i>: If anyone else is interested, the kickstarter is set to end tomorrow (Monday) at 11 pm EDT","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","user":"One Vorlon","date":". 07-19-2015, 05:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-24T21:19:50-07:00","id":602540,"title":"","content":"Damn, I meant to pledge and forgot. I hope they expand the world a bit this time. IIRC, first edition had 3 countries: accepting liberal good guy land, ruled by an elite who passed a flawless morality test; well-meaning but hidebound conservative theocracy land; and Undead-Mordor.<br /> <br /> Edit: I found my pdf I bought years ago! There is also a noble-shamanistic-warrior-nomad Khanate. (which makes sense given that Blue Sword is a major influence)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 07-25-2015, 12:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T03:46:13-07:00","id":603707,"title":"","content":"There's also the Roamers, a Romani-equivalent (since fantasy-Romani pop up in romantic fantasy), and the Matriarchy of Lar'tya, introduced in the &quot;World of Aldea&quot; supplement, a caste-based island kingdom 1400 miles southwest of Aldis.<br /> <br /> Thanks to the Kickstarter, the new edition's going to introduce some micro-settings, capsule settings about 2000 words long, some of which are pretty far-flung from the established setting (one's implied to be on another world altogether).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}